## 283 - Move All Zeros to end

## Approach
Approach:
1. I use two pointers, i and j.
2. j goes through the complete array and searches for non-zero elements.
3. i keeps track of the position where the next non-zero element should be placed.
4. Whenever arr[j] is not zero, I swap arr[i] and arr[j], then increase i.
5. At the end, all non-zero elements come to the front and all zeros
   automatically move to the end.

Example:
[0,1,0,3,12]

After moving non-zero elements:
[1,3,12,0,0]

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public void moveZeroes(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int i = 0;
        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            if (nums[j] != 0) {
                int temp = nums[i];
                nums[i] = nums[j];
                nums[j] = temp;
                i++;
            }
        }
    }
}
